<p><b>Wednesday.</b> All three detectors separate brute force; DBSCAN (F1 {{ n.wed_db_f1_4 }}) matches the port rule (F1 {{ n.wed_port_f1_4 }}) at fewer false alerts per day ({{ n.t2_wed_dbscan_fa }} against {{ n.t2_wed_port_sample_fa }}) for {{ n.t2_wed_dbscan_labels }} analyst labels, while K-Means raises {{ n.t2_wed_kmeans_fa }} per day (F1 {{ n.wed_km_f1_3 }}). <b>Thursday.</b> F1 is {{ n.thu_km_f1 }} (K-Means), {{ n.thu_gmm_f1 }} (GMM) and {{ n.thu_db_f1 }} (DBSCAN); the zero-payload rule scores {{ n.t5_thu_payload_f1 }} on the same sample with no labels.</p>
