<p><b>Stability.</b> On Thursday the detectors lie within {{ n.thu_spread }} F1 and their seed ranges overlap ({{ n.thu_overlap_lo }}–{{ n.thu_overlap_hi }}), so they cannot be ranked. F1 moves most with triage size for K-Means ({{ n.t6_thu_kmeans_triage_n_span }}), PCA dimension for DBSCAN ({{ n.t6_thu_dbscan_pca_dims_span }}) and sample size for GMM ({{ n.t6_thu_gmm_sample_size_span }}); analyst error up to {{ n.sw_analyst_error_2 }} moves it by at most {{ n.sw_err_max }}. Only {{ n.t2_thu_db_valid }} of {{ n.t2_thu_db_all }} Thursday DBSCAN settings meet the noise cap, and F1 spans {{ n.t2_thu_db_fmin }}–{{ n.t2_thu_db_fmax }}.</p>

<!-- ======================================================= 4 CRITICAL REFLECTION -->
<h1 id="s4">Critical reflection</h1>
<h2 id="s4-1">Where each technique added value and fell short</h2>
<p class="lead"><b>Supervised, value.</b> RF is near-perfect on a campaign it has seen: on {{ n.sp_wed80 }} F1 {{ n.t3_wed80_rf_f1 }} at {{ n.t3_wed80_rf_fa }} false alerts per day, the lowest point estimate there (LogReg {{ n.t3_wed80_lr_fa }}, port rule {{ n.t3_wed80_port_fa }}; the MLP's {{ n.t3_wed80_mlp_fa }} [{{ n.t3_wed80_mlp_fa_lo }}–{{ n.t3_wed80_mlp_fa_hi }}] overlaps). Brute-force flows are easy to separate: the median found brute-force flow has {{ n.w_med_pps_att }} packets/s and a {{ n.w_med_win_att }}-byte initial window, against {{ n.w_med_pps_ben }} and {{ n.w_med_win_ben }} for benign. <b>Shortfall.</b> RF is blind to an unseen attack type (recall {{ n.t3_wed70_rf_recall }} on {{ n.sp_wed70 }}; the port rule {{ n.t3_wed70_port_recall }}). On infiltration it flags {{ n.thu_benign_flagged }} of benign traffic at threshold {{ n.c_thr }}, and a threshold chosen on validation for at most {{ n.c_budget }} false alerts per day gives {{ n.thu_op_fa }} on test ({{ n.thu_op_x }}× the budget, recall {{ n.thu_op_recall }}) against {{ n.thu_op_val_fa }} on validation: the budget does not transfer between windows (distribution shift).</p>
<p class="lead"><b>Unsupervised, value.</b> Wednesday brute force is separated without labels: DBSCAN reaches F1 {{ n.wed_db_f1_4 }} at {{ n.t2_wed_dbscan_fa }} false alerts per day for {{ n.t2_wed_dbscan_labels }} analyst labels, GMM F1 {{ n.wed_gmm_f1_4 }}. <b>Shortfall.</b> The selection criteria are unstable at the grid edges. GMM BIC never turns by {{ n.g2_gmm_wed_hi }} components on Wednesday. DBSCAN silhouette keeps rising past min_samples {{ n.t2_wed_db_ms }}: it goes from {{ n.t2_wed_ext_sil0 }} to {{ n.t2_wed_ext_sil1 }} (min_samples {{ n.t2_wed_ext_ms }}) on Wednesday and from {{ n.t2_thu_ext_sil0 }} to {{ n.t2_thu_ext_sil1 }} ({{ n.t2_thu_ext_ms }}) on Thursday, while F1 falls from {{ n.t2_wed_ext_f0 }} to {{ n.t2_wed_ext_f1 }} and from {{ n.t2_thu_ext_f0 }} to {{ n.t2_thu_ext_f1 }}. The label-free choice is not settled.</p>

<h2 id="s4-2">What was found and what was missed (infiltration)</h2>
<p><a class="ref" href="#tab-7">Table 7</a> compares the groups. <b>(a) Most clustering finds are reproducible by one line.</b> The zero-payload rule catches {{ n.t7_found_pay }} of the {{ n.t7_found_n }} flows any detector found ({{ n.t7_found_pay_share }}); the port rule catches {{ n.t7_found_port }}. <b>(b) The interesting finds are the single-algorithm ones no rule reproduces.</b> The GMM-only ({{ n.t7_onlygmm_n }}) and DBSCAN-only ({{ n.t7_onlydb_n }}) groups are long, near-silent connections (median {{ n.t7_onlygmm_dur }} and {{ n.t7_onlydb_dur }} µs); the payload rule catches {{ n.t7_onlygmm_pay }} and {{ n.t7_onlydb_pay }} of them, the port rule {{ n.t7_onlygmm_port }} and {{ n.t7_onlydb_port }}. <b>(c) Missed flows look like benign traffic.</b> {{ n.t7_missed_nn }} of the {{ n.t7_missed_n }} flows missed by all have mostly benign neighbours, against {{ n.t7_found_nn }} of found flows; their top ports are {{ n.port_p53 }}, {{ n.port_p443 }} and {{ n.port_p3389 }} ({{ n.port_p53_share }}, {{ n.port_p443_share }}, {{ n.port_p3389_share }}). <b>(d) Label noise caps any flow-level detector.</b> {{ n.t7_allatk_dup }} of all sampled infiltration flows ({{ n.t7_found_dup }} of the found ones, {{ n.t7_missed_dup }} of the missed) are feature-identical to a benign flow, because infiltration labels are assigned by host and time window [3]. It does not separate found from missed but explains why found clusters carry false alerts.</p>
